    "lawCode": "Amd §104, Pub Off L",
    "lawSection": "Public Officers Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S2754\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to amend the public officers law, in relation to requiring\nposting of notice of meetings on the internet\n\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF THE BILL :\n\nThe bill amends the Public Officer's Law to require that, when a\npublic body has the ability to do so, notice of the time and place of\na meeting given in accordance with subdivisions one or two of said\nlaw, shall he conspicuously posted on the public body's internet\nwebsite.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1 of section 104 of the Public Officer's Law is amended by\nadding a new subdivision (5) which states that when a public body has\nthe ability to do so, notice of the time and place of a meeting given\nin accordance with subdivision one or two of this section, shall also\nhe conspicuously posted on the public body's internet website.\n\nSection 2 provides for the bill to be effective immediately.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nInstitutions and organizations charged with the responsibility of\nserving the general public should he required to make the necessary\narrangements to allow for as much transparency and openness in their\ndeliberations as possible.  Seeing as how said institutions typically\nmaintain active internet websites, and that a considerable segment of\nthe public use such websites to keep informed, they should be\ncomprehensively updated and revised as frequently as possible.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nA.7642 of 2005-2006\nA.4053/S.4567 of 2007-2008.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately.\n",
